ciation of the  people that are going to be wearing the  clothes was very very moving paul was  certainly a new kid on the block because  i used so many of the same people over  and over again film after film but i  love paul's work he designed all the  costumes for hamilton and i really  wanted to work with him on this  [Music]  with stephen's help with the help of the  entire creative team and tony kushner  like i've been able to find something  really new inside of her and who this  character is  at the end of dance in the gym i  couldn't believe i was never going back  to that high school i would never see  that gym again it was so sad he remains  a student he remains curious and when  he's not working he tells me he's just  studying footage here's a guy who just  loves what he does and you know that  really was infectious for everyone it  allowed everyone to kind of come and  approach the material from the same  mentality of  just chasing your joy we had a blast it  was early in the schedule and dance in  the gym help us realize the kind of  movie we were making this is the end of  dancing  i love it that's fantastic america goes  to a lot of different places he saw it  in the script and talked about oh my  goodness america is a challenge it  starts in the apartment but then it goes  and travels through the entire  neighborhood so we had a series of large  street sets  [Music]  took 10 days to shoot america and there  was a heat wave it just became part of  the feel part of the character of the  song to have to perform this very  vibrant empowering song when it's like  hot sweltering summer day  [Music]  it's always an added challenge when  you're on location but my goal is always  to make it sound real  whenever you're doing a live piece of  music you have to use wireless earpieces  they do pre-records before we're doing a  scene and those pre-records will play  back into their ear pieces when we start  filming we'll do a few pieces to play  back so the actors